WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.080
Oh.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.440
This one is yours, too.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:17.600
You sound surprised.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.040
I suppose I am.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.840
It's not at all like the
others you donated, is it?

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.200
It is not.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.080
The others are…

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.720
Well, they were
to my father's tastes.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.640
If Lady Danbury is to be
believed,

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.560
this one was
a favourite of my mother's.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.120
I have never understood why.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.600
It is very beautiful.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.480
It reminds me of

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.640
waking up in the country.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.760
First thing in the morning.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:58.680
When I'm all alone.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.120
And I've not yet spoken to
a soul.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.680
I look outside the window
and it is…

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.560
serene.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.200
It's as if I could be
the only person left

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.640
in the world and yet

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:16.240
somehow I am not lonely.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:18.800
I am comforted.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:19.880
At peace.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.920
The others are certainly

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.080
very grand
and impressive but,

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:25.880
this one…

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.160
This one is intimate.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.600
It's been a pleasure
working with you, comrade.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.720
Pleasure's mine.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:15.920
Wait, wait! Wait!

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:19.320
Really?

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.240
That's it?

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.880
You're just gonna walk away
like this never happened?

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:27.800
Well that's what
professionals do, right?

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:29.920
Sarah, I've just had
the best day of my life.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.560
John B, you're gonna blow
our cover.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:34.840
Look, I don't care about
my cover, Sarah.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.880
I don't care
if my friends find out

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.200
or your boyfriend
with his frosted tips.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.360
Look, yesterday I didn't
even know who you were.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:44.760
And, today, I'm like…

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.000
Sarah Cameron.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:52.280
And, honestly, in my limited
experience, that's rare.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.800
That's, like, eclipse rare.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.080
Like a blind person

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.720
seeing colour
for the first time rare

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.560
or, like, Bigfoot evidence
or the Northern Lights.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.280
Look, I can't pretend like
this isn't real,

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.920
like this didn't happen.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.680
-I'm sorry. I--
-Shut up.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:15.760
I can't pretend, either.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.760
Hey, man, get a room.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.040
What are you gonna tell
Jackson?

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.680
-Diarrhoea attack.
-God.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.200
He's never gonna speak to me
again, is he?

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.960
Why didn't you say goodbye?

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.680
I was letting him
off the hook.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.240
They're not gonna want
their golden boy

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.840
dating someone
like me anyway so,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.920
why go through
the fate stuff?

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:58.920
Yeah, well.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:03:59.960
If you don't open
yourself up,

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:00.920
you're never gonna find out.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:01.840
No.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:05.000
-No therapy, remember.
-What? Oh. Sorry.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:10.800
You all right?

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:12.760
I've got a jumper.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.520
So chivalrous.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:17.280
Well, actually,

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.280
there's some Nutella
on it, so not exactly.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.200
Great.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.680
Why are your arms
so freakishly long?

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:32.480
They're not.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:35.800
Just roll up your sleeves,
you fool!

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:39.640
This one.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.280
I'm a virgin!

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:53.960
-What?
-I…

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.640
I'm a virgin,

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.680
and I thought you should
know that I am.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:04:59.240
Yeah, that's totally cool.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.240
-No judgement.
-Cool.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.720
Glad I shared.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.120
I'm gonna head off now.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:08.440
Oh. Ok.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:09.440
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.400
Strange time to practice.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.160
But better late than never.

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:24.120
I swear I'm not a stalker.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.680
I just really had to talk
to you.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.160
How'd you find me?

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.200
Do you even have to ask?

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.560
Elsa tracks my phone.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.400
First off,

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.400
it sucks you're avoiding me.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.080
I put myself out there

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:51.520
and I was honest with you

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:54.520
and for that I get
the silent treatment?

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.200
Even if you don't feel
the same,

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:01.520
you could at least be there
for me as a friend.

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:04.360
You're making me feel crazy!

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:09.200
Honestly,

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.400
if I knew

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.720
that you were gonna be
all weird

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.040
and that this was gonna
jeopardise our friendship,

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:17.840
I never in a million years

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:19.040
would have told you
how I felt.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:23.080
Because it is becoming
incredibly clear that

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.600
you don't feel the same way.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.120
Aleksander--

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.600
I have been fighting
this war

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:49.960
alone for so long.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:54.280
I've buried so many

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:56.080
good soldiers,

00:06:58.360 --> 00:06:59.360
friends.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:02.960
The coffers are running dry.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.440
The noose tightens.

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:10.360
And our own people
are turning against Grisha,

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:11.360
just as their kin once did.

00:07:31.960 --> 00:07:33.200
You are not alone.

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:47.720
I've been waiting
a long time for you.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:54.680
I should go.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:57.640
You lied to me
from the very beginning.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:00.800
You used me as a way to keep
your brother alive.

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.040
I didn't lie to you.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.920
I just… I couldn't tell you
everything right away.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.320
Mildred!

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:07.880
You lied.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.960
Until the lie
didn't serve you anymore.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:12.120
Then you decided to
tell the truth.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.360
And I understand that

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.520
the world has not been kind
to you

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.160
and I am sorry for that,
I truly am.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:18.440
But that doesn't give you
the right

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:21.320
to dissemble at
every possible opportunity

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:22.320
to the people around you

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:23.720
whose only mistake was
to care about you.

00:08:23.800 --> 00:08:25.200
I know that.

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:26.280
Do you?

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.040
Because I honestly
don't think that you do.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:29.800
My feelings for you
are real.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:30.880
I don't think

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.960
that you have any idea
what your feelings are.

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:37.600
Because you have been lying
for so long.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:40.320
It's second nature to you.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:41.680
You even lie to yourself.

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:44.920
Well, your lying
and your selfishness

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.840
have cost me everything.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.080
I don't know
what my life is anymore.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.400
I don't understand
how I got so

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.280
tangled up in you.

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:55.440
And I don't understand

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:57.720
whether my feelings for you
are real

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.120
and you waltzed into
my heart

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.600
and I cannot get you out.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:01.680
Gwendolyn.

00:09:02.280 --> 00:09:03.640
I love you.

00:09:03.720 --> 00:09:04.760
Gwendolyn.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.200
I don't even know what
I'm supposed to say to that.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.480
And, anyway,

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.680
I don't believe you!

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.200
What I kept from you,

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.760
that was not easy
for me to do.

00:09:28.760 --> 00:09:30.920
I wanted to tell you
everything.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.120
And I understand how awful
that would make you feel.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:36.440
How used you must have felt.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:40.760
The lies I told to get into
that hospital,

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:43.000
to get closer to Edmund,

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.680
those were amoral acts and I
understand that completely,

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:50.200
but you must understand that
I had no choice.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:54.360
And, if I had to, I would do
it all over again.

00:09:56.640 --> 00:10:00.480
I wish you could leave the
pain I've caused behind us.

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:04.520
Let go of the resentment,
the suspicion.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:08.160
My feelings for you are
the truest thing in me.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:10.920
I love you. Do you hear me?

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.280
I love you.

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:19.880
What are you doing here?

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:22.640
So this is your room, huh?

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.080
Yes, and why are you in it?

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:26.600
Do you like him, Hunter?

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:27.800
Why are you here?

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:30.000
Do you like him?

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:31.160
Yeah, I do.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:33.400
Ok, then.

00:10:34.280 --> 00:10:35.160
That's that.

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.240
That's what?

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.720
I'm just Maxine's
dumb friend, remember?

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:42.080
Who climbs through a window?

00:10:42.160 --> 00:10:44.160
This isn't some rapey
John Hughes mo--

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:46.640
What the hell was that?

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:48.080
Who kisses someone
right after

00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:49.400
they use the word rapey
in a sentence?

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:51.200
Sorry, it's just I know you
were on that date tonight

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:52.680
and Maxine won't shut up
about how perfect

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:53.840
you and Hunter are

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.400
and I can't stop thinking
about you.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:58.600
The other day
when you grabbed me--

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:10.960
Is he here now?

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:18.720
No.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:22.640
Good.

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:25.440
Because, you know,

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:27.400
I'll sort him out for you
if I have to.

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:31.160
Oi.

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:32.840
Dead boyfriend!

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:34.840
Give it up, mate! It's over.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:42.480
Who is he, Poppins?

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:45.320
How are you still standing?

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:50.320
I think I'm crazy.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:53.360
I think you're surprisingly
sane, considering.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:57.160
Look.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:00.920
I know what it feels like.

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:03.800
You feel like
you can't find--

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:11.000
Are you sure?

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:14.080
Yes.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:31.800
Ok.

